BEGIN_DESC
Io, evening (the Sun ~12 deg up in the west, sunset in ~1.4 h): the heavy suit "Pantsir" (class 2) on the frost plain ~5 m from the front of an active pahoehoe lobe, southern margin of the Prometheus flow field (1.785 S, 153.616 W), facing west.
The Sun goes down behind the Prometheus plume (vent ~70 km W, lng 155.8 W): a ballistic SO2 gas-and-frost umbrella 80 km high, optically thin and scattering forward, so it is brightest now, looking into the Sun. At the vent the Sun stands ~2 deg higher than here.
Behind her (NE): the glowing breakout toes, glassy fresh crust with glowing cooling cracks, a lava tube with skylights up to a small lava shield (~95 m) with a crusted lava lake. Temperatures: 1-D cooling model of 1450 K basalt in vacuum (Tantra_Design/io_lava, Config/Io/LavaField). Pantsir nominal is +430 C, the floating limit ~550-600 C.
~9 m SSW, on the frost plain out of the lava's heat: the EMPU, headlights off, and Kaira Rean in the Suit_T10 (set Boron) with the Hexa flight module, facing the volcano. Jupiter is below the horizon on this side of Io (no eclipse).
Morning version: "Io - Pantsir lava field".
END_DESC

